#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:1
msgid "Kernel Families"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:3
msgid ""
"GPU kernels are frequently specialized for different problem shapes, "
"hardware capabilities, resource limits, or tuning decisions. A single "
"logical operation may therefore have several ahead-of-time compiled entry "
"points."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:7
msgid ""
"`KernelFamily` represents such a set of compiled variants and provides a "
"validated host-side selection mechanism."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:10
msgid "It separates two independent decisions:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:12
msgid ""
"Eligibility: can this variant safely execute this problem?\n"
"Preference:  which eligible variant should execute?\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:17
msgid ""
"This distinction is important. Performance policy must never select a "
"variant that violates its launch, shape, hardware, or resource requirements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:20
msgid ""
"`KernelFamily` performs selection entirely on the CPU. It does not compile "
"kernels, query CUDA devices, benchmark entries, create threads, or access "
"the filesystem. The application supplies all relevant problem and hardware "
"facts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:24
msgid "When to use a kernel family"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:26
msgid ""
"Use `KernelFamily` when an operation has a small, fixed set of already "
"compiled implementations, such as:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:29
msgid "different output tile sizes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:30
msgid "different block dimensions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:31
msgid "specialized tensor-core kernels for particular compute capabilities"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:32
msgid "small-input and large-input implementations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:33
msgid "kernels with different shared-memory requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:34
msgid "kernels tuned for different problem-shape ranges"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:35
msgid "a generic fallback plus one or more optimized variants"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:37
msgid ""
"A kernel family is not a runtime registry or a JIT compiler. Its number of "
"variants is a const generic and is therefore part of the Rust type:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:40
msgid "KernelFamily<Id, Entry, Meta, const N: usize>\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:44
msgid "The family owns exactly `N` variants."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:46
msgid ""
"This bounded representation is useful when the available kernels are "
"determined at build time and should remain explicit and auditable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:49
msgid "Selection model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:51
msgid "The selection flow has two modes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:53
msgid ""
"Force(id) -> resolve variant -> validate ----------------------> Override\n"
"\n"
"Auto      -> cache lookup -> resolve -> validate --------------> Cache\n"
"          -> filter eligible variants\n"
"          -> selector chooses an ID\n"
"          -> validate selector output\n"
"          -> cache selected ID --------------------------------> Selector\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:63
msgid ""
"`SelectionMode::Force(id)` is a validated manual override. It bypasses the "
"cache and selector, but it does not bypass eligibility validation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:66
msgid ""
"`SelectionMode::Auto` first attempts to use a cached stable variant ID. "
"Unknown or newly ineligible cache entries are treated as misses. The "
"selector then sees only eligible variants."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:70
msgid "Every successful selection reports its provenance:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:72
msgid ""
"pub enum SelectionSource {\n"
"    Override,\n"
"    Cache,\n"
"    Selector,\n"
"}\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:80
msgid ""
"This lets applications distinguish operator overrides, cached decisions, and "
"new selector decisions in logs and diagnostics."
msgstr ""

