#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:1001
msgid "Design guidelines"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:1003
msgid "Use the following rules when introducing a new family."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:1005
msgid "Keep the family bounded"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:1007
msgid "Prefer a small set of meaningful compiled variants."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:1009
msgid ""
"A large dynamically changing set usually indicates that a registry, "
"generated dispatch table, or tuning database is a better abstraction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:1012
msgid "Make IDs semantic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:1014
msgid ""
"The ID should describe which compiled contract is selected, not where it "
"happens to appear in an array."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:1017
msgid "Put correctness in eligibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:1019
msgid ""
"Any condition required for safe or correct execution belongs in "
"`KernelProblem::validate`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:1022
msgid "Do not rely on the selector to avoid unsafe variants."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:1024
msgid "Put performance in preference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:1026
msgid "The selector should decide among already valid choices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../gpu-programming/kernel-families.md:1028
